The graph of a cumulative distribution function is shown below.

\exfigure{323_q30_1}

The curved section of the graph is part of the function $y = \dfrac{(x - 1)^3}{6}$

solutions.latex:
\exfigure{402_q20_s1}

$f(x)$ is a parabola on $0\le x\le2$, symmetric about its axis $x=1$, and the mode is at $x=1$. Half of the total area lies on each side of $x=1$, so the median is also $1$.
$$\therefore\ \text{median}=\text{mode}=1$$

